{"time": "20261117T173048Z", "think": "", "command": "answer The Deepest Hall is done. I killed Hesh-Var for the Bronze Key, then killed the wraith Lord of Vorannuhl and took the third Seal-Stone of the Kings from the Household Hoard. I now carry all three stones (Blackrose, Gemin, Kings), about 350 gold, Reel-Ka armour, rapier, 2 lockpicks, 3 paralysis poisons, sap jar, keystone, eye-setting. Next: bring the stones to Never-Writes-Twice in Nesh-Deeka's House in Helstrom before anyone goes near the Kings Gate under Teku-Sul Spire (dive from Bell Station). Do not lift the Eye: used in place at the Root it strengthens the trees, but lifted it cuts every tree off from the others. Rivals are the Unbound and the Collector Ennodius Vanin at Blackrose. Still open: why the Unbound drain trees, what moans in the Fort Chalkmoth cellar, and how Nesh-Deeka knows about the Unbound.", "refused": true, "result": "Refused: every command needs --think.", "summary": null}
